review_comments.body:
Agent-drafted and reviewed by Manoel.

blocking: Responses `instructions` are lost when `input` is missing

This PR adds `"instructions"` to the keys left out of `$ai_model_parameters` (line 338). However, `GetInputFromRequest` only turns it into a system message inside the `requestJson["input"] != null` branch (lines 585–614). It also returns early for a `prompt` before reaching that branch.

`input` is optional in the Responses API, for example with `previous_response_id`, `conversation` or a stored `prompt`. In those requests the system prompt is now in neither `$ai_input` nor `$ai_model_parameters`. Before this PR it was at least captured in `$ai_model_parameters["instructions"]`, so this is a regression from the merge-base.

This is the same concern dustinbyrne raised on #400 (https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-dotnet/pull/400#discussion_r4672128668). #400's branch fixes it in `d5b67a1`, but this PR is stacked on the older `c5e4a15`.

Reproduction test, saved as `tests/PostHog.AI.Tests/PrReviewInstrDiagTests.cs`:
```csharp
#pragma warning disable CS0618
using System.Net;
using System.Text;
using System.Text.Json;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using NSubstitute;

namespace PostHog.AI.Tests;

public sealed class PrReviewInstrDiagTests
{
    [Fact]
    public async Task InstructionsKeptWhenInputAbsent()
    {
        var ph = Substitute.For<IPostHogClient>();
        Dictionary<string, object>? captured = null;
        ph.Capture(Arg.Any<string>(), Arg.Any<string>(), Arg.Do<Dictionary<string, object>>(d => captured = d), Arg.Any<GroupCollection?>(), Arg.Any<bool>(), Arg.Any<DateTimeOffset?>());
        using var h = new PostHogOpenAIHandler(ph, Substitute.For<ILogger<PostHogOpenAIHandler>>()) { InnerHandler = new Stub() };
        using var client = new HttpClient(h) { BaseAddress = new Uri("https://api.openai.com") };
        var req = new { model = "gpt-5", instructions = "You are a pirate.", previous_response_id = "resp_1" };
        using var c = new StringContent(JsonSerializer.Serialize(req), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");
        using var r = await client.PostAsync(new Uri("/v1/responses", UriKind.Relative), c);
        var hasMp = captured!.TryGetValue(PostHogAIFieldNames.ModelParameters, out var m) && ((Dictionary<string, object>)m).ContainsKey("instructions");
        Assert.True(captured.ContainsKey(PostHogAIFieldNames.Input) || hasMp, "instructions absent from both $ai_input and $ai_model_parameters");
    }

    private sealed class Stub : HttpMessageHandler
    {
        protected override Task<HttpResponseMessage> SendAsync(HttpRequestMessage request, CancellationToken ct) =>
            Task.FromResult(new HttpResponseMessage(HttpStatusCode.OK) { Content = new StringContent("{\"id\":\"resp_2\",\"object\":\"response\",\"model\":\"gpt-5\",\"output\":[],\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":1,\"total_tokens\":2}}", Encoding.UTF8, "application/json") });
    }
}
```
Run: `dotnet test tests/PostHog.AI.Tests -f net8.0 --filter "FullyQualifiedName~PrReviewInstrDiagTests"`

Reproduction: reproduced — the test above failed twice on head `013cacc` with "instructions absent from both $ai_input and $ai_model_parameters", and passed on merge-base `ea79fc9`.
